import{_ as i,o as t,c as o,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 290 | Shrouding-the-Heavens Decomposition | Inevitable Historical Regression: Emperor Falls = Dark Turmoil","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 290 | Shrouding-the-Heavens Decomposition | Inevitable Historical Regression: Emperor Falls = Dark Turmoil","no":290,"module":2,"tags":["Shrouding the Heavens","Dark Turmoil","Emperor Falls","Historical Regression","Oligarchic Civilization"],"related":["05-Myriad Races Common Progress Basic Program","07-Self-Generated Self-Growing Evolution Law","04-Anti-Predation Core Thesis"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0290_模块2-遮天-历史倒退必然性.md","filePath":"en/0290_模块2-遮天-历史倒退必然性.md"}'),s={name:"en/0290_模块2-遮天-历史倒退必然性.md"};function r(a,e,l,h,u,d){return t(),o("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="entry-290-shrouding-the-heavens-decomposition-inevitable-historical-regression-emperor-falls-dark-turmoil" tabindex="-1">Entry 290 | Shrouding-the-Heavens Decomposition | Inevitable Historical Regression: Emperor Falls = Dark Turmoil <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-290-shrouding-the-heavens-decomposition-inevitable-historical-regression-emperor-falls-dark-turmoil" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 290 | Shrouding-the-Heavens Decomposition | Inevitable Historical Regression: Emperor Falls = Dark Turmoil&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Full Decomposition of the Shrouding-the-Heavens System (Entry 3) | Benchmark base: Documents 05, 07, 04</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-between-prosperity-and-chaos-lies-only-one-person-s-nirvana" tabindex="-1">Introduction: Between prosperity and chaos lies only one person&#39;s nirvana <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-between-prosperity-and-chaos-lies-only-one-person-s-nirvana" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: Between prosperity and chaos lies only one person&#39;s nirvana&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Among the six top-level axioms, the causal self-discipline axiom requires rooting out civilization regression and historical backsliding; the collective ascension axiom requires strong ones to feed back to Myriad Ranks. This entry dissects the Shrouding-the-Heavens world&#39;s cruelest law — <strong>the day an emperor enters nirvana is the start of civilization regression</strong>. The law-first axiom requires us to treat this &quot;law&quot; as a setting-level hard flaw, not tragic aesthetics. Protagonist uniqueness dependency = medium (oligarchic civilization). The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s evaluation base has been upgraded to six top-level axioms.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Energy waste behind historical regression is &quot;protection vacuum&quot; waste:</p><ul><li>Emperor present, cosmos-tier suppression energy covers the starry sky; emperor dies, this energy instantly zeroes out, rather than precipitating into institutions</li><li>Quasi-emperor, Great Sage tier strong ones slaughter each other over legacy before and after the emperor falls; protection energy consumed in civil war</li><li>Energy that could maintain order all consumed in the long chaos of &quot;waiting for the next emperor to be born&quot;</li></ul><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This is this entry&#39;s core; Shrouding-the-Heavens&#39; regression is a structural iron law:</p><ol><li><strong>Suppression-vacuum law</strong>: what the emperor suppresses is not specific enemies, but &quot;the space for strong ones to do evil.&quot; The person leaves, the space opens</li><li><strong>Dark-turmoil cycle law</strong>: whenever ancient supremes, forbidden-land dark beings feel lifespans ending, they harvest lives to extend; civilization population cliff-drops</li><li><strong>Knowledge extinction law</strong>: in turmoils aristocratic families, Dao legacies are blood-washed; cross-eon accumulated cultivation knowledge batch-buried</li><li><strong>Population and civilization double drop</strong>: every dark turmoil is a population-zero, civilization-restart regression</li></ol><p>Shrouding-the-Heavens&#39; &quot;history&quot; is not an upward line, but an oscillating loop of &quot;rise — turmoil — zero — re-rise&quot; — every oscillation does not guarantee returning to the previous height.</p><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Ye Fan himself ended his era&#39;s dark turmoils, but his predatory thinking manifests in:</p><ul><li><strong>&quot;I decide&quot; path dependency</strong>: solving turmoils is &quot;I am stronger, I suppress,&quot; not &quot;build institutions that do not depend on my suppressing&quot;</li><li><strong>Avoiding turmoil roots</strong>: forbidden lands, ancient supremes, lifespan anxiety — these structural lesions are not rooted out, only temporarily held down by Ye Fan&#39;s personal force</li><li><strong>Treating chaos as backdrop</strong>: dark turmoils in narrative are the protagonist&#39;s sharpening stone, not civilization problems needing institutional solutions</li></ul><p>It is worth emphasizing: Shrouding-the-Heavens&#39; regression is not that chaos is worse than prosperity, but that every prosperity is shorter than the previous. This is the oscillating loop&#39;s true horror: after turmoil, civilization energy may not return to pre-turmoil height, because knowledge generational break, population loss, Dao-legacy severance superimpose, making rebuilding lose its starting point. The causal self-discipline axiom writes rooting out civilization regression and historical backsliding into the top level precisely because it sees through oscillating civilization&#39;s essence — it seems to cycle, actually declines. Ye Fan ended his era&#39;s turmoils, but did not institutionally cut this downward spiral; the world after him only pushed the spiral back a few generations.</p><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Shrouding-the-Heavens Turmoil Logic</th><th>Anchor Symbiosis Alternative</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Emperor seated = peace; emperor dead = chaos</td><td>Alaya whole-network supervision, early-warning without any person seated</td></tr><tr><td>Ancient supremes harvest lives to extend</td><td>Life-circulation system public, severing &quot;must take lives&quot; path</td></tr><tr><td>Turmoil = population zero</td><td>Civilization error-correction engineering, turmoil nipped in the bud by institutions</td></tr><tr><td>Institution absent, hero relied on</td><td>Anchor Council legislates, order does not depend on any emperor</td></tr><tr><td>Regression periodic</td><td>Causal self-discipline axiom roots out historical backsliding</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: replicate dark-turmoil timeline and population-energy curve</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: inject three groups of &quot;Ye Fan in office suppressing,&quot; &quot;Ye Fan nirvanas,&quot; &quot;Alaya supervision connected&quot;</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: turmoil eruption interval, death toll per turmoil, time for civilization energy to recover pre-turmoil</li><li><strong>Review</strong>: quantify &quot;oligarchic protection&quot; fragility — as long as the suppressor is absent, regression probability approaches one</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Setting self-consistency: medium-low</strong>. Dark-turmoil causes (lifespan, forbidden lands) early logic self-consistent; late for the protagonist&#39;s sake, forbidden-land count and ancient-supreme strength fluctuate with plot</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk: medium-high</strong>. Turmoil scale varies large and small, entirely by how grim plot needs to render</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency: medium</strong>. Whether turmoil ends depends on whether Ye Fan&#39;s personal force covers the whole</li></ul><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: suppression energy zeroing with the person&#39;s death is the biggest energy waste</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: ancient supremes taking lives to extend is naked stock predation</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo world&#39;s regression depends on &quot;is Tang Luo present,&quot; Shrouding depends on &quot;is the emperor present,&quot; structurally homologous, but Shrouding bloodier</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: in turmoil all Myriad Ranks are leeks to be cut, no one has institutional protection</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: oscillating civilization cannot support cross-plane, cross-multiverse stable connection</li><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power is inherent in all; the easygoing retain a guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin erases predatory motivation, predatory involution loses meaning from the root</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>&quot;Emperor falls = dark turmoil&quot; is not Shrouding-the-Heavens&#39; world-view highlight, but its setting bankruptcy proof — a world that builds civilization safety on &quot;don&#39;t let the strong one die&quot; writes regression into the calendar from day one.</p><p>In the final analysis, Shrouding-the-Heavens · inevitable historical regression described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./296_模块2-遮天-黑暗动乱解析.html">Entry 296 · Dark Turmoil Analysis</a> · <a href="./297_模块2-遮天-大帝制度批判.html">Entry 297 · Emperor Institution Critique</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/05-万族共进基本纲领.html">05-Myriad Races Common Progress Basic Program</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',29)])])}const p=i(s,[["render",r]]);export{g as __pageData,p as default};
